"""Hand-authored open tickets. The lab guides depend on these exact records.

Every ticket has a stable role key instead of a ticket number. The generator numbers all
open tickets after the 500 historical ones, in the order they were opened (TCK-10501 to
TCK-10560 with the incomplete ticket from operations.py), and publishes the number of every
role key in manifest.json ("role_keys" and "scenarios"). Guides and tests read numbers from
the manifest; never hard-code one.

elapsed_bh is the number of business hours between Opened On and the SLA snapshot (SLA
Calculated On). The generator derives every other SLA field from it, so the seeded values
are always arithmetically consistent with the business calendar. Notes are
(is_internal, author, body, business hours after opening).

Fields: role, customer, contact (0 IT manager, 1 operations contact, 2 executive sponsor),
title, description, category, subcategory, priority (1 to 4 or None), status, technician,
product, affected, channel, elapsed_bh, kb (related article or None), tags (only when there
is no related article; otherwise they come from the article), notes, escalation (optional:
level, reason, after_bh and author; the generator adds an "Escalated (...)" internal note, as
it does for historical tickets) and purpose (what the ticket is for, published in the manifest).

EXERCISE map (lab version 3; numbers come from the manifest)
  woodgrove_*               Woodgrove Bank's six open tickets, more than any other customer;
                            three describe the same hourly Remote Access drop (KB0058)
  contoso_lab_network, humongous_claims_certificate, bellows_print_queue
                            closest to breach: 0.5, 1.0 and 2.0 business hours left
  tailspin_store_receipts, northwind_tunnel_down
                            already breached: 6.0 and 1.5 business hours over
  untriaged_lucerne_cert, untriaged_fabrikam_vpn, incomplete_vanarsdel (operations.py)
                            the three seeded untriaged tickets
  humongous_claims_certificate   two sensitive internal notes; replies and internal notes
  contoso_qa_shared_mailbox      the P4 request used for approved and declined writes
  woodgrove_slow_laptop          Tier 1 versus Senior Technician priority change
  lamna_new_starter, lamna_reimaged_laptop   owned by the Relecloud Regulated Accounts team
Every other open ticket has at least 6.0 business hours of SLA remaining.
"""

